🪐
"Orbits"/en
=== start
¶Three planets circling a star that pulls them around.¶

¶The star does the pulling, so it needs @Matter with a pull. It has no @Motion,
so nothing pulls it back and it stays where it is. A @Place is an output's
corner rather than its middle, so the star is shifted by half its own size to
put its middle at the center of the sky.¶
sun: Phrase(
	'⭐️' 2m
	name: 'sun'
	place: Place(-1m -1m)
	matter: Matter(2000kg pull: 1)
)

¶A planet needs no @Matter at all. Having a @Motion is what lets the star's pull
move it. How fast it must travel to circle instead of falling in depends on how
far out it is, so each planet is given the speed that holds its own ring.¶
planet: ƒ(glyph•"" called•"" wide•#m far•#m speed•#m/s)
	Phrase(
		glyph wide
		name: called
		place: Motion(
			Place(far - (wide ÷ 2) 0m - (wide ÷ 2))
			Velocity(0m/s speed)
		)
	)

¶The sky has no gravity of its own, or everything would fall out of the bottom.
It has no air either, so the planets keep going instead of slowing to a stop.¶
Stage(
	[
		sun
		planet('🌍' 'earth' 0.8m 3m 11.5m/s)
		planet('🪐' 'ringed' 1m 5m 8.6m/s)
		planet('🌕' 'moon' 0.6m 7m 7.3m/s)
	]
	background: Color(15% 20 300°)
	gravity: 0m/s^2
	air: 0
	place: Place(0m 0m -14m)
)
